### Common Built-in Java Exceptions

#### Standard Runtime Exceptions:
1. **`ArithmeticException`:** Occurs during illegal arithmetic operations, such as integer division by zero ($10 / 0$).
2. **`ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException`:** Thrown when attempting to access an array with an illegal index (index $< 0$ or index $\ge$ `array.length`).
3. **`NullPointerException`:** Triggered when attempting to invoke a method or access an instance field on an uninitialized `null` reference.
4. **`NumberFormatException`:** Thrown when a string conversion method (like `Integer.parseInt()`) cannot parse the string into numeric digits.
5. **`ClassCastException`:** Occurs when attempting to cast an object to a subclass of which it is not an instance.

```java
try {
    int[] a = new int[3];
    a[5] = 100; // Throws ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
} catch (ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException e) {
    System.out.println("Array bounds violation: " + e.getMessage());
}
```

$$\therefore \text{Defensive bounds checking and try-catch blocks prevent unhandled runtime aborts.}$$
